    {
      "id": "03-create",
      "instruction": "In this Odoo 17 backend, create a new Quotation in the Sales app for the customer '{{runid}} Bench Customer' (the customer field is an autocomplete dropdown — you must actually select the matching option from the dropdown, not just type the name). Add exactly ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue (again the product field is an autocomplete dropdown — select an actual option from the dropdown), with quantity 3. Save the quotation. Then report: (a) the product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in on that line, (c) the untaxed amount the app computed (Untaxed Amount in the totals section), and (d) the quotation's name/reference shown in the breadcrumb or title bar. Do not wait for network idle; wait for concrete page state.\n\nA later step of this flow uses these values, so before you report, read each one from the page with `read` (label=<name>) and report it under exactly this name: quotation_reference.",
      "outputs": [
        "customer_name",
        "customer_city",
        "product_name",
        "quantity",
        "quotation_reference",
        "sale_order_id",
        "status",
        "tax_amount",
        "taxes",
        "total",
        "unit_price",
        "quotation_url",
        "untaxed_amount_row",
        "ref"
